        "topic": "Modular Arithmetic",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the remainder when $17$ is divided by $5$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In modular arithmetic, $17 \\mod 5$ is the remainder when $17$ is divided by $5$. Since $5 \\times 3 = 15$ and $17 - 15 = 2$, the remainder is $2$.</p>",
