        "explanation": "<p>Using the Pythagorean identity, $\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$. Thus, $\\cos^2 \\theta = 1 - \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2 = 1 - \\frac{9}{25} = \\frac{16}{25}$. Therefore, $\\cos \\theta = \\pm \\frac{4}{5}$. Since no quadrant is specified, we consider the positive value.</p>",
